Narrator: You kneel down to inspect it closer, running your fingers over the carved-in stone.
Noelle: (One, two, three degrees.) #portrait:NoelleSkeptical
Noelle: These are wayfinding shorthands. For when the weather makes it too hard to see, and we have to figure out the direction on our gears… #portrait:NoelleSkeptical
Noelle: (But why would they be on the walls of a ruin?) #portrait:NoelleSkeptical
Chione: None of us would’ve recognised it for that… #portrait:ChioneHm
Noelle: They’re meant to be read from touch, after all. #portrait:NoelleUm
Amelia: If it’s a language from your homeland… #portrait:AmeliaNeutral
